        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/display/main/gui/womo_connectivity_modal.c#L36-L36",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b188cb2fedf1a46cdfb670b2ecc924c2d1a571ac158d4fc30f0bbcbfd080e343:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b95086f7a86d470c96df1674be5d79bb",
      "statement": "The AP/HotSpot column in the connectivity modal is purely informational with no on/off switch, showing SSID, connected client count, and a device list (hostname from DHCP lease, fallback MAC); the AP must never be disabled by software because it is the sole communication channel between the ESP32 boards and the router, and no code path in womo_connectivity_modal.c, womo_router_uci.c, or the standalone router-webui tool provides a way to disable it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/display/CLAUDE.md#L48-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d61f5a4f613bfd9a7e04d4c52dffae59b87176d632c9031d511b452d749c3ee0:"
