    {
      "id": "claim_0ceeae5942c44d01919d9a923f89dc77",
      "statement": "deploy.sh installs the router-webui tool under /etc/womo/ instead of /www because on the RUTX11 /www is a read-only SquashFS mount with no overlay, while only /etc/ is backed by the writable JFFS2 overlay; it serves the content via a dedicated second uhttpd instance (uhttpd.womo) on port 8080 rather than the stock web root, and appends /etc/womo/ to /etc/sysupgrade.conf so RutOS's settings-keep mechanism (which otherwise only preserves /etc/config/* and the standard package list) preserves it across firmware sysupgrades.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://tools/router-webui/deploy.sh#L1-L21",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a9865c719c8d91cd80accd5c771f3becb1f00e1f3b5f12a23feb3765ef639e65:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tools/router-webui/deploy.sh#L416-L436",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:927de50e4f4d829cba61dd18b8b112c34fc0d51c0b13febe5180727a5aad9781:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_681cc5decf6d45788f5db27643f2fc91",
      "statement": "deploy.sh installs CGI proxy scripts under /etc/womo/cgi-bin/ (ubus reverse-proxy to localhost, lte wrapping gsmctl, clients parsing iwinfo assoclist + dhcp.leases, simswitch triggering sim_switch, datapass scraping pass.telekom.de over the qmimux0 LTE interface) plus a poll.sh that writes AP/Wi-Fi/LTE/GPS status atomically to /etc/womo/status.json, driven by a cron job running poll.sh every 15s and datapass.sh every 30 minutes plus once at boot via /etc/rc.local.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://tools/router-webui/deploy.sh#L383-L414",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:522a60cb8b8f30e03e6d6ace1d1d8d225871f2f2e42e892fbedf1d8539a3f9f1:"
        },
